<title>FRANCE: France sees lower 96 sugar beet crop - ministry.</title>
<headline>France sees lower 96 sugar beet crop - ministry.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French farm ministry predicted on Friday a 3.6 percent drop in the 1996 sugar beet harvest, mostly the result of lower yields.</p>
<p>In its first estimate for the new season, the ministry said France would harvest 29.3 million tonnes of sugar beets in 1996 against 30.4 million tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The forecast assumes the national beet yield would drop to 64.3 tonnes per hectare from 66.3 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>Area sown to sugar beets was put at 456,000 hectares, barely unchanged from 458,000 hectares last year.</p>
<p>Beet sugar content was put at 17.2 percent against 17.5 percent. --Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
